@scene chapter_4_quartermasters_caravan

background: green_valley.jpg
music: mystery_forest.mp3

dialogue:
"The forest opens onto a trade road, and the trade road is a disaster."
"A caravan sits stranded — wagons half-loaded, crates strewn across the verge in no order at all."
"A broad, grizzled man stamps up and down the line, counting on his fingers and swearing at them."

background: quartermaster

npc Quartermaster:
"Nine! No — eight. BAH."
"Every crate in the wrong wagon, every wagon in the wrong place."
"The Blight came through and scrambled my whole manifest. Now the satchels can't remember what sits WHERE."

dialogue:
"He notices you standing there."

npc Quartermaster:
"You. You've got the look of someone the System still talks to. Make yourself useful."

system notification:
"NEW QUEST"
"THE QUARTERMASTER'S CARAVAN"
"Restore order to the caravan's satchels."

npc Quartermaster:
"A satchel isn't a HEAP, traveller. It's a LINE."
"First slot, second slot, third — order kept, always. That's a list. Things in a row, and the row remembers."

dialogue:
"He upends a satchel. Crates tumble out and snap into a neat, numbered line."

npc Quartermaster:
"And here's what trips up every soft-handed hero the System sends me."
"The satchel counts from ZERO. Slot zero is the FIRST crate. Ask me for the third, I reach into slot two."
"Reach past the end and it SCREAMS at you. 'Index out of range.' I hear it in my nightmares."

dialogue:
"He shoves a loaded satchel into your arms."

npc Quartermaster:
"Travellers count like people. Satchels count from zero. Mind the gap between the two."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Return the crate a traveller asks for — remembering the satchel counts from 0."

mission: caravan_lists

background: green_valley.jpg

dialogue:
"You reach into slot after slot, each one place lower than the number asked."
"Crate after crate lands in its proper wagon. The line remembers itself."
"The Quartermaster watches, arms folded, and grunts what might — in a generous light — be approval."

npc Quartermaster:
"Huh. You counted from zero and didn't fall off the end. More than the last six managed."
"But you've only READ from the line. You haven't packed one, or pulled from the back, or taken a whole run of crates in one reach."
"Stay a while. There's more to a satchel than pointing at it — and the archivist up the road will expect you to know all of it."

dialogue:
"He is already dragging another satchel over, and does not appear to be asking."

system level_up:
"CHAPTER COMPLETE"
"The Quartermaster's Caravan"
"Applied: lists · indexing from zero · order"

reward:
xp: 100
gold: 45
achievement: KEEPER OF ORDER

next:
chapter_4b_satchel_of_slots
